  "question": {
    "text": "The atomic number of elements <math> <mrow> <mtext>A,&nbsp;B,&nbsp;C</mtext></mrow> </math> and <math> <mtext>D</mtext> </math> are <math> <mrow> <mtext>Z</mtext><mo>−</mo><mtext>1,&nbsp;</mtext><mtext> </mtext><mtext>Z,&nbsp;</mtext><mtext> </mtext><mtext>Z</mtext><mtext> </mtext><mtext>+</mtext><mtext> </mtext><mtext>1,&nbsp;</mtext><mtext> </mtext><mtext>Z</mtext><mtext> </mtext><mtext>+</mtext><mtext> </mtext><mtext>2</mtext></mrow> </math> respectively. If <math> <mtext>B</mtext> </math> is a noble gas, choose the correct option<br />\r(i) <math> <mrow> <mtext>(A)</mtext></mrow> </math> has higher electron affinity<br />\r(ii) <math> <mrow> <mfenced> <mtext>C</mtext> </mfenced></mrow> </math> exists in + 2 oxidation state<br />\r(iii) <math> <mrow> <mfenced> <mtext>D</mtext> </mfenced></mrow> </math> is an alkaline earth metal",
    "image": null
  },
