  "correctValue": null,
  "solution": {
    "text": "Atomic number of  <math><mfenced separators=\"|\"><mrow><mi>B</mi></mrow></mfenced><mo>=</mo><mi>Z</mi><mi> </mi></math>  and is a noble gas<br/><br/>Atomic number of  <math><mfenced separators=\"|\"><mrow><mi>A</mi></mrow></mfenced><mo>=</mo><mi>Z</mi><mo>-</mo><mn>1</mn></math>   (i.e., is a Halogen)<br/><br/>Atomic number  <math><mfenced separators=\"|\"><mrow><mi>C</mi></mrow></mfenced><mo>,</mo><mo>=</mo><mi>Z</mi><mo>+</mo><mn>1</mn></math> (i.e., is a alkali metal)<br/><br/>At number of  <math><mfenced separators=\"|\"><mrow><mi>D</mi></mrow></mfenced><mo>=</mo><mi>Z</mi><mo>+</mo><mn>2</mn></math>  (i.e., alkaline earth metal)<br/><br/>Hence, element  <math><mfenced separators=\"|\"><mrow><mi>A</mi></mrow></mfenced></math>  must be a Halogen, so has highest electron affinity among the given species.  <math><mfenced separators=\"|\"><mrow><mi>C</mi></mrow></mfenced><mo>.</mo></math>  is an alkali metal and  <math><mfenced separators=\"|\"><mrow><mi>D</mi></mrow></mfenced></math>  is an alkaline earth metal",
